.TH WAYEXPAND 1 "September 2026" "WayExpand 1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wayexpand \- validate and manage WayExpand text-expansion configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wayexpand
.I COMMAND
\&[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
WayExpand is a local Wayland text expander. The daemon performs expansion;
this command provides setup, status, editing, diagnostics, certification,
configuration management, and configuration validation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Interactively choose a compatibility mode and activate the safest available
path after displaying session capabilities and safety tradeoffs. Use
--mode recommended|maximum|experimental and --yes for reviewed automation.
.TP
.B edit [CONFIG]
Open the graphical snippet editor.
.TP
.B status [--json]
Show the active daemon status. The JSON form is stable for automation.
.TP
.B doctor [--json] [CONFIG]
Report available input and output backends and their compatibility.
.TP
.B certify [--json]
Produce a machine-readable local certification report. Protocol availability
is not treated as end-to-end certification; untested scenarios remain visible.
.TP
.B test TEXT [--json] [CONFIG]
Simulate input and report matching expansions without starting the daemon.
.TP
.B test-hotkey CHORD [--json] [CONFIG]
Resolve a hotkey without executing its action.
.TP
.B preview TRIGGER [--json] [CONFIG]
Preview a replacement, optionally with an application context.
.TP
.B list [--json] [CONFIG]
List configured expansions and hotkeys.
.TP
.B search QUERY [--json] [CONFIG]
Search configured triggers, descriptions, and tags.
.TP
.B validate CONFIG
Parse and validate a configuration file without starting the daemon.
.TP
.B backup [CONFIG] [DESTINATION]
Create a private, non-overwriting configuration backup.
.TP
.B backend
Show implementation and environment status for backend paths.
.TP
.B explain-backend
Explain the expert backend selection decision and its tradeoffs.
.TP
.B portal status|reset
Inspect or forget the stored libei portal restoration token. Resetting the
local token may cause the portal to ask for access again; it does not revoke a
portal grant already held by another session.
.TP
.B help | version
Show command help or print the installed version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/wayexpand/expansions.toml
Per-user expansion configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wayexpand.sock
User control socket used by the daemon and GUI.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I /usr/share/doc/wayexpand/
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/itchyitchy123/wayexpand/issues.
